<##
$$
W
  ====
  - [[Page~134 甲(8)]]
    ==
    - The plumula or scaly covering of a growing seed,
      the budding forth of a plant;
    - a sprout or bud;
    - the first of the 'ten stems;'
      _met._ the first, number one, the head, excellent, the best---\
      from the common use of the 'stems' as ordinal numbers;
    - to begin, to get the start of;
    - to excel, to surpass;
    - armor for the body, a cuirass, a corselet;
    - military;
    - applied to the hard defensive covering of animals,
      as the carapace of turtles, the elytra of beetles,
      the large scaly plates on some fishes,
      the finger nail, &c.;
    - graduates of the degree of _tsinsz'_ [[進士]];
    - the first on a tripos paper
      is called _(2)ting k(a/)p(8)_ [[ding2 gaap3]];
    - _k(a/)p(8) ~~(u:)t(8)~~ ``(u:)t(9)``_
        [[gaap3 jyut6]]
        the first and second of the 'ten stems,'
        are used hypothetically for persons,
        like "J.~Doe and R.~Roe;"
    - _(2)h(e/)ung k(a/)p(8)_
        [[hoeng2 gaap3]]
        jingling scales hung to the girdle of actors;
    - _k(a/)p(8) (2)ch(e/)ung_
        [[gaap3 zoeng2]],
        headman of a tithing;
    - _k(a/)p(8) ~~ch(')(a/)k(9)~~ ``ch(')(a/)k(8)``_
        [[gaap3 caak3]]
        a bud, a sprout;
    - _luk(9) k(a/)p(8)_
        [[luk6 gaap3]]
        the gravid uterus;
    - _k(a/)p(8) (1)ping_
        [[gaap3 bing1]],
        cavalry.
    ==
  ====
$$
